    "problem_statement": "Query.load() returns None instead of self\n\n#### Description\n\nThe `Query.load()` method is returning `None` instead of returning `self`, breaking method chaining and causing various operations to fail.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom furl import furl\n\n# This should work but returns None\nf = furl.furl()\nresult = f.query.load('a=1&b=2')\nprint(result)  # prints None instead of the Query object\n\n# Method chaining is broken\nf = furl.furl()\ntry:\n    f.query.load('a=1&b=2').add('c=3')\nexcept AttributeError as e:\n    print(f\"Error: {e}\")  # 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'add'\n\n# Basic query loading doesn't work as expected\nf = furl.furl()\nf.query.load('a=1&b=2')\nprint(f.query)  # Shows incomplete query parameters\n```\n\nThe `load()` method should return `self` to allow method chaining and maintain consistency with other methods in the API."
  }
